-- (2) pair. Fields: spouses who live together; parent and child who live together; the child's age; a child not a foster child under parental control of a non-parent; the child is under 18
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(2) the pair is treated as customarily purchasing and preparing meals together` (`s 2012(m)(2) pair` OF TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- "Spouses who live together"
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(2) the pair is treated as customarily purchasing and preparing meals together` (`s 2012(m)(2) pair` OF FALSE, TRUE, 21, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- "parents and their children 21 years of age or younger": 21 is within
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(2) the pair is treated as customarily purchasing and preparing meals together` (`s 2012(m)(2) pair` OF FALSE, TRUE, 22, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING  -- 22 is outside; paragraph (2) deems only these pairs
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(2) the pair is treated as customarily purchasing and preparing meals together` (`s 2012(m)(2) pair` OF FALSE, FALSE, 10, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- "children (excluding foster children) under 18 years of age who live with and are under the parental control of a person other than their parent"
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(2) the pair is treated as customarily purchasing and preparing meals together` (`s 2012(m)(2) pair` OF FALSE, FALSE, 10, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING  -- the child is not under 18
-- (3) individual. Fields: 60+; lives with others; unable to purchase and prepare; certified; income of the others; poverty line
`a 65 year old who cannot cook, others earn 1650 against a line of 1000` MEANS `s 2012(m)(3) individual` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 1650, 1000
`a 65 year old who cannot cook, others earn 1651 against a line of 1000` MEANS `s 2012(m)(3) individual` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 1651, 1000
`a 59 year old who cannot cook`   MEANS `s 2012(m)(3) individual` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 100, 1000
`a 65 year old not certified`     MEANS `s 2012(m)(3) individual` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 100, 1000
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(3) the individual is considered an individual household with the spouse` `a 65 year old who cannot cook, others earn 1650 against a line of 1000` EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- "does not exceed the poverty line ... by more than 65 per centum": 1650 is exactly 165 percent
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(3) the individual is considered an individual household with the spouse` `a 65 year old who cannot cook, others earn 1651 against a line of 1000` EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- 1651 exceeds 165 percent of 1000
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(3) the individual is considered an individual household with the spouse` `a 59 year old who cannot cook` EQUALS NOTHING  -- not sixty: paragraph (3) does not reach them
#ASSERT `s 2012(m)(3) the individual is considered an individual household with the spouse` `a 65 year old not certified` EQUALS NOTHING  -- no physician's certificate: paragraph (3) does not reach them
